{"author":{"id":"8022379585b4ab99ca8775db3eb67d33fcb256817114c28e51ccc1e9f55cdec4"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1792310785,"nonce":"/QNMbhqL+J6XfHGMjK+Av7tykMU=","title":"CLOSED 2026-08-04: raising the pool past the P-cluster on Alder Lake (NUE_MATMUL_WORKERS=16 vs default 8) gives prefill -7.9% but decode ...","message":"`Q4Matmul.workerCount()` = `CpuTopology.perfCoreCount()` — \"never past the\nP-cluster … that slack keeps a co-runner (or the OS) from preempting a spinning\nworker\". On the 4P+8E i5-1250P that is 8 workers on a 16-thread box, with the\n8 E-cores idle. llama.cpp gains +8% prefill going t=8 -\u003e t=16, so this looked\nlike free money.\n\nPage cache warmed first, `.rayzor` swept + `--no-cache` per arm, interleaved,\nBOTH phases from the same run:\n\n| | prefill TTFT | decode |\n|---|---|---|\n| pair1 W=8 | 99.996 s | **5.52 tok/s** |\n| pair1 W=16 | 77.503 s | 4.70 |\n| pair2 W=8 | 83.153 s | **7.30** |\n| pair2 W=16 | 76.163 s | 5.02 |\n| pair3 W=8 | 82.565 s | **7.04** |\n| pair3 W=16 | 76.614 s | 4.62 |\n\n**prefill -7.9% (3/3) but decode -33% (3/3).** Medians 83.15 -\u003e 76.61 s and\n7.04 -\u003e 4.70 tok/s.\n\nPrefill is ONE-SHOT (saves ~6.5 s once); decode runs for the whole session.\nTrading 33% of decode for 7.9% of prefill is a large net loss.\n\n**The `workerCount()` comment was right and is now measured.**\n\nMy first reading was `-5.6%, 2/2 pairwise` — **prefill only**. On that basis I\nwas about to recommend flipping a default that costs 33% of decode.\n**When a knob changes thread/core policy, measure BOTH phases in the SAME run.**\nA prefill-only A/B cannot see a decode cliff.\n\n`SpinPool.parallelRows` already work-steals with chunked claims (\"~8 claims per\nworker … leaving enough grains for stealing to absorb slow cores\"), so slow\nE-cores are absorbed, not gating. The cost is DISPATCH OVERHEAD: decode issues\n~224 dispatches per token (7 matmuls x 32 layers), and doubling workers doubles\nper-dispatch wake/barrier cost while each worker's share shrinks toward zero.\nConsistent with [[perf_attention_split_measured_ffn_is_the_lever]]: decode is\ndominated by fixed per-token cost, pool already ~89% utilised.\n\nPhase-dependent worker counts (16 for prefill, 8 for decode) would need either\ntwo pools (24 spinning threads) or participation gating, for a one-shot 6.5 s.\nNot worth it.\n\n---\nArchived from Claude memory `perf_ecore_workers_measured_decode_cliff` on 2026-10-18. A record of past work; open items in it may have their own issues.","files":null}]}